// ================================================================
// TREE LEVEL DEFINITIONS (UnplannedProjectScreen)
//
// Level 0 : Workspace
//      - Contains all root projects.
//      - Multiple root project cards are displayed together.
//
// Level 1 : Root Project
//      - A single root project card.
//      - Example:
//          Android Development
//
// Level 2 : First Child of the Root Project
//      - Acts as the workspace heading.
//      - This is the first expandable section.
//      - Example:
//          UI Layer
//
// Level 3 : Child of Level 2
//      - First level displayed inside the breadcrumb.
//      - Example:
//          Compose
//
// Level N : Child of Level (N-1)
//      - Continues recursively.
//      - Example:
//          Components → Buttons → Primary Button ...
//
// Leaf Node
//      - Any node with no children.
//      - Leaf nodes NEVER become:
//          • Workspace Heading
//          • Breadcrumb
//          • Expanded Workspace
//      - Leaf nodes are actionable work items only.
//      - They display session controls, completion toggle,
//        notes, statistics, etc.
//
// Navigation Rules
//      Level 0 -> All root projects remain visible.
//      Level 1 -> Root project card expands.
//      Level 2 -> Becomes the workspace heading.
//      Level 3+ -> Displayed in the breadcrumb.
//      Leaf -> Never changes navigation state.
// ================================================================